# Spotify Developer app client ID (from https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard).
# This project uses PKCE, not the client-credentials flow, so no client secret is
# ever needed — see .claude/SECURITY.md.
#
# Register exactly ONE redirect URI in the dashboard — used by both the host's own
# login and a top-tracks-mode player's login (see .claude/DECISIONS.md ADR-005):
#   https://vdwolde.github.io/Song-Snitch/callback.html
# That page is public/callback.html in this repo — it publishes automatically with
# every GitHub Pages deploy (Vite copies public/ into the build verbatim), not deployed
# separately. Neither a loopback nor a LAN address is ever registered with Spotify.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=cf927e357a0b4485b77310b99e3fb3a2

# PORT / BIND_LAN / UI_ORIGIN are NOT read from this file — Start-Project.bat and
# `npm run dev` already set them as real shell environment variables, which is required:
# they're read at module-import time, before a .env file would be loaded.
